      "items": [
        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "As a Developer, I want a reusable {{product-card-group}} React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it can render a labelled group of product cards across multiple pages including PDP, PLP, and Homepage.\n\nThe component renders an optional section header (title + link) and a responsive row of ProductCard components (SFCC-236). It does not own the product data or navigation logic — it receives a product array, title, and link label as props. Whether the underlying data comes from SFCC merchandising logic, a Contentful-curated editorial slot, or a personalisation engine is irrelevant to the component.\n\n_Props in scope:_\n\n||Prop||Values||Notes||\n|display|3, 4, 6|Controls number of product cards rendered|\n|size|Desktop, Mobile|Controls layout breakpoint|\n|showTitleAndLink|true, false|Toggles the entire section header|\n|showLink|true, false|Independently toggles the link within the header; only applies when showTitleAndLink=true|\n|title|string|Section heading text|\n|linkLabel|string|Link text e.g. Shop All, View More|\n\nExamples of usage: More from this category and Recommended for you on the PDP.",
          "to_string": "As a Developer, \nI want a reusable {{product-card-group}} React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, \nso that it can render a labelled group of product cards across multiple pages including PDP, PLP, and Homepage.\n\n----\n\nThe component renders an optional section header (title + link) and a responsive row of ProductCard components (SFCC-236). It does not own the product data or navigation logic — it receives a product array, title, and link label as props. Whether the underlying data comes from SFCC merchandising logic, a Contentful-curated editorial slot, or a personalisation engine is irrelevant to the component.\n\n_Props in scope:_\n\n||*Prop*||*Values*||*Notes*||\n|display|3, 4, 6|Controls number of product cards rendered|\n|size|Desktop, Mobile|Controls layout breakpoint|\n|showTitleAndLink|true, false|Toggles the entire section header|\n|showLink|true, false|Independently toggles the link within the header; only applies when showTitleAndLink=true|\n|title|string|Section heading text|\n|linkLabel|string|Link text e.g. Shop All, View More|\n\nExamples of usage: More from this category and Recommended for you on the PDP."
        }
      ],
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-21T14:41:48.683000+10:00"
    },
    {
      "items": [
        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "1. Given the component is rendered with a valid display prop, when it mounts, then the correct number of ProductCard instances are rendered matching the display value.\n2. Given showTitleAndLink=true and showLink=true, when the component renders, then the section header displays both the title and the link using the linkLabel value.\n3. Given showTitleAndLink=true and showLink=false, when the component renders, then the title is displayed but no link is shown.\n4. Given showTitleAndLink=false, when the component renders, then neither the title nor the link are displayed.\n5. Given the component is rendered with an empty or missing product array, when it mounts, then it renders no product cards and no error is thrown.\n6. Given the component is rendered at size=Desktop or size=Mobile, when it mounts, then the layout matches the corresponding Figma design spec variant.\n7. Given the section header is visible, when rendered, then the title is a semantically correct heading element and the link is a native anchor element with descriptive text.\n8. Given the component is interactive, when a keyboard user navigates to the link, then it is reachable and activatable via keyboard alone.\n9. Given the component renders product cards, when a screen reader traverses the group, then each card is distinguishable and the group is appropriately labelled.",
          "to_string": "1. Given the component is rendered with a valid display prop, when it mounts, then the correct number of ProductCard instances are rendered matching the display value.\n2. Given showTitleAndLink=true and showLink=true, when the component renders, then the section header displays both the title and the link using the linkLabel value.\n3. Given showTitleAndLink=true and showLink=false, when the component renders, then the title is displayed but no link is shown.\n4. Given showTitleAndLink=false, when the component renders, then neither the title nor the link are displayed.\n5. Given the component is rendered with an empty or missing product array, when it mounts, then it renders no product cards and no error is thrown.\n6. Given the component is rendered at size=Desktop or size=Mobile, when it mounts, then the layout matches the corresponding Figma design spec variant.\n7. Given the section header is visible, when rendered, then the title is a semantically correct heading element and the link is a native anchor element with descriptive text.\n\nAccessibility\n8. Given the component is interactive, when a keyboard user navigates to the link, then it is reachable and activatable via keyboard alone.\n9. Given the component renders product cards, when a screen reader traverses the group, then each card is distinguishable and the group is appropriately labelled.\n10. Given the component is rendered, when tested against WCAG 2.1 AA criteria, then it passes with no violations.",
          "from_id": "",
          "to_id": ""
        }
      ],
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
