        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "# Given Einstein Recommendations has been provisioned in BM, when a business user navigates to recommendation zone configuration, then zones can be created and assigned to each required surface (PDP, Cart, Mini-Bag, My Account).\n# Given recommendation zones have been configured, when the configuration is saved, then a Recommended for You zone exists and is correctly named for each of the following surfaces: PDP, Cart, Mini-Bag, and My Account.\n# Given recommendation zones have been configured, when the configuration is saved, then a More from Category zone exists and is correctly named for the PDP surface.\n# Given Einstein has insufficient behavioural data for a zone, when the surface renders, then rules-based fallback recommendations are served instead of Einstein-powered results.\n# Given a recommendation zone has been configured in BM, when a merchandiser toggles between AI-driven and rules-gated logic, then the change takes effect without a code deployment.",
          "to_string": "# Given Einstein Recommendations has been enabled in BM, when a developer navigates to the recommendation zone configuration, then the feature is active and zones can be created.\n# Given zones are required for Recommended for You, when provisioning is complete, then named zones exist for PDP, Cart, Mini-Bag, and My Account surfaces.\n# Given a zone is required for More from Category, when provisioning is complete, then a named zone exists for the PDP surface.\n# Given zones have been provisioned, when a developer inspects each zone in BM, then the zone names match the naming convention agreed with the PWA team for API calls.",
