        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "# Given Einstein Recommendations has been provisioned in BM, when a business user navigates to recommendation zone configuration, then a zone can be created and assigned to each required surface (PDP, Cart, My Account).\n# Given recommendation zones have been configured, when the configuration is saved, then each zone has a distinct, correctly named identifier and is assigned to the correct surface — including separate zones for YMAL and Complete the Look on the PDP.\n# Given rules-based fallback logic has been configured in BM, when Einstein has insufficient behavioural data to drive recommendations, then the fallback rules are applied and products are returned.\n# Given AI-driven vs rules-gated logic is configurable by season and category in BM, when a business user updates the configuration, then the correct logic is applied to the relevant surface without a code deployment.",
          "to_string": "# Given Einstein Recommendations has been provisioned in BM, when a business user navigates to recommendation zone configuration, then zones can be created and assigned to each required surface (PDP, Cart, Mini-Bag, My Account).\n# Given recommendation zones have been configured, when the configuration is saved, then a Recommended for You zone exists and is correctly named for each of the following surfaces: PDP, Cart, Mini-Bag, and My Account.\n# Given recommendation zones have been configured, when the configuration is saved, then a More from Category zone exists and is correctly named for the PDP surface.\n# Given Einstein has insufficient behavioural data for a zone, when the surface renders, then rules-based fallback recommendations are served instead of Einstein-powered results.\n# Given a recommendation zone has been configured in BM, when a merchandiser toggles between AI-driven and rules-gated logic, then the change takes effect without a code deployment.",
