      "items": [
        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "As a Site Merchandiser,\n\nI want Einstein Recommendations provisioned and recommendation zones configured in Business Manager,\n\nso that all recommendation surfaces across the storefront have a reliable foundation to build against before any PWA carousel work begins.\n\nThis story covers all BM-side configuration for recommendations: Einstein provisioning, recommendation zone setup per surface (YMAL, Complete the Look), rules-based fallback logic at launch, and the ability to toggle between AI-driven and rules-gated logic by season and category. This is a hard prerequisite for Search – Recommendations – You May Also Like Carousel and Search – Recommendations – Complete the Look — neither can be built or tested until recommendation zones are configured.\n\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\n\n# Given Einstein Recommendations has been provisioned in BM, when a business user navigates to the recommendation zones configuration, then all required surfaces (PDP, Cart, Mini-Bag, My Account) are available to configure.\n# Given recommendation zones have been configured per surface in BM, when the configuration is saved, then each surface has a distinct, correctly named zone assigned to it.\n# Given rules-based fallback logic has been configured in BM, when Einstein has insufficient behavioural data to drive recommendations, then the fallback rules are applied and products are returned.\n# Given AI-driven vs rules-gated logic is configurable by season and category in BM, when a business user updates the configuration, then the correct logic is applied to the relevant surface without a code deployment.\n\n*Open Items / Dependencies:*\n\n@Mani Ramachandran: Confirm Einstein Recommendations is provisioned in the SFCC sandbox and all required zones are available for configuration.\n\n@Izzy Chaloner: Confirm the rules-based fallback logic and product selection criteria to be applied at launch before sufficient behavioural data accumulates.\n\n@Izzy Chaloner: Confirm which seasons and categories require rules-gated logic vs AI-driven logic at launch.",
