          "from_string": "*As a* Shopper, \n\n*I want* product cards to display relevant information for the surface I am browsing, \n\n*so that* each page feels appropriately tailored without inconsistent component implementations across the site.\n\n----\n\n*Images for reference (Figma is leading):*\n\n!image-20260727-234551.png|width=486,alt=\"image-20260727-234551.png\"!\n\n\n\nThis story covers the build of a single shared Product Card component that supports multiple display variations via a style prop. Each variation controls which elements are shown — the component itself is built and maintained once. The component is scoped to the visual and interactive layer only — product data is sourced from SFCC. \n\nVariations in scope: \n\n* Homepage: image, name, badge — no cart/wishlist icon, no size selector, price (desktop hover only)\n* PLP: image, name, price, badge, cart icon, size selector (desktop hover only), out-of-stock state. \n* Wish List: image, name, colour, size, price, cart icon, badge, 'x'\n\nAdditional variations follow the same pattern and can be added",
          "to_string": "*As a* Shopper, \n\n*I want* product cards to display relevant information for the surface I am browsing, \n\n*so that* each page feels appropriately tailored without inconsistent component implementations across the site.\n\n----\n\n*Images for reference (Figma is leading):*\n\n!image-20260727-234551.png|width=486,alt=\"image-20260727-234551.png\"!\n\n\n\nThis story covers the build of a single shared Product Card component that supports multiple display variations via a style prop. Each variation controls which elements are shown — the component itself is built and maintained once. The component is scoped to the visual and interactive layer only — product data is sourced from SFCC. \n\n*Variations in scope:* \n\n* Homepage\n* PLP\n* Wish List"
        }
