648	   * Wishlist) — see docblock point 6. Unlike every other reveal in this file, this one is NOT
649	   * gated behind a `ZimmProductCardStyleProps` flag: `baseStyle({})` with no props at all must
650	   * still emit it, because desktop arrows behave identically across every variation whenever a
651	   * card has more than one image. `zimmProductCardMedia.css.ts`'s own `carousel` part used to
652	   * reveal itself unconditionally under its own `[HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY]` block (a device-
653	   * CAPABILITY check, making arrows permanently visible on any hover-capable device) — that
654	   * sub-block is now removed entirely (see that file's own regression guard), so this pair is the
655	   * only reveal path left for the arrows.
656	   */
657	  test('carousel arrows: unconditional hover+focus-visible reveal inside HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY, present even with no other flags set', () => {
658	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({});
659	    const root = style.root as Record<string, unknown>;
660	    const hoverBlock = root[HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY] as Record<string, unknown>;
661	    // Fix J (SFCC-236): `display: 'flex'` is kept here (unlike every other reveal in this file,
662	    // which drops `display` entirely) — carousel needs it for its own `justifyContent`/
663	    // `alignItems` layout, since `zimmProductCardMedia.css.ts`'s own unconditional `display: 'none'`
664	    // is gone. `clipPath: 'none'` is the actual reveal signal now, added alongside it.
665	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_CAROUSEL_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).display).toBe('flex');
666	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_CAROUSEL_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('none');
667	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_CAROUSEL_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).display).toBe('flex');
668	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_CAROUSEL_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('none');
669	  });
670	
671	  /**
672	   * Fix J belt-and-braces (SFCC-236) — see zimmProductCard.css.ts docblock point 6's own Fix J
673	   * note: once the carousel wrapper's hidden state stops being `display: 'none'` (which removed
674	   * the whole subtree from hit-testing regardless of any descendant's own `pointerEvents`), its
675	   * arrow buttons' own unconditional `pointerEvents: 'auto'` (zimmProductCardMedia.css.ts's
676	   * `arrowButton` part) is no longer guaranteed un-hittable while clipped, so this recipe adds an
677	   * explicit default-off/reveal-on pair targeting the buttons themselves.
678	   */
679	  test('carousel arrow buttons: pointerEvents is none by default and auto only once revealed (Fix J belt-and-braces)', () => {
680	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({});
681	    const root = style.root as Record<string, unknown>;
682	    expect((root[CAROUSEL_BUTTON_LIFT_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).pointerEvents).toBe('none');
683	    const hoverBlock = root[HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY] as Record<string, unknown>;
684	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_CAROUSEL_BUTTON_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).pointerEvents).toBe('auto');
685	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_CAROUSEL_BUTTON_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).pointerEvents).toBe('auto');
686	  });
687	
688	  /**
689	   * Fix 1 (Scorer rework round 1): the close-button lift rule used to also set
690	   * `position: 'relative'`, which is what an earlier version of this exact test asserted for all
691	   * three lift keys together. That was proven wrong by rendering the real composed tree: Media's
692	   * own `close` recipe part already sets `position: 'absolute', top: 0, right: 0` on this exact
693	   * element, and this rule's `.css-root [data-card-slot="close"]` descendant+attribute selector
694	   * has higher specificity than Media's own single-class rule — so `position: 'relative'` here
695	   * WON the cascade and knocked the remove button out of its pinned top-right corner into normal
696	   * flow. The element is already positioned (by Media's own recipe), which is all `zIndex` needs
697	   * to take effect — a competing `position` value here was never necessary. See the DOM-level
698	   * proof below (real recipes composed through the real `chakra` factory + `getComputedStyle`)
699	   * for confirmation the fix actually restores the pinned position, not just that this key's shape
700	   * looks right in isolation.
701	   */
702	  test('the close lift selector sets only zIndex, never position — the element is already positioned by ZimmProductCardMedia’s own recipe', () => {
703	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({});
704	    const root = style.root as Record<string, unknown>;
705	    const closeLift = root[CLOSE_LIFT_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>;
706	    expect(closeLift.zIndex).toBe(1);
707	    expect(Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(closeLift, 'position')).toBe(false);
708	  });
709	
710	  /**
711	   * Fix I (SFCC-236, found via live mobile-device touch-swipe testing after this branch's own
712	   * live testing round): the media/gallery scroll region itself was never added to this lift
713	   * list, even though it is exactly as interactive as the controls nested inside it — a touch
714	   * swipe starting on the image landed on the invisible overlay `<a>` first, and the real scroll
715	   * container underneath never received the gesture. Same shape as the close/carousel lift keys
716	   * above: ZimmProductCardMedia's own root recipe already sets `position: 'relative'`, so only
717	   * `zIndex` is needed here — plus `cursor: 'pointer'`, since this element is no longer inside the
718	   * `<a>` that used to convey that affordance via the browser's default link cursor.
719	   */
720	  test('the media lift selector sets zIndex and cursor:pointer, never position — the element is already positioned by ZimmProductCardMedia’s own recipe', () => {
721	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({});
722	    const root = style.root as Record<string, unknown>;
723	    const mediaLift = root[MEDIA_LIFT_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>;
724	    expect(mediaLift.zIndex).toBe(1);
725	    expect(mediaLift.cursor).toBe('pointer');
726	    expect(Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(mediaLift, 'position')).toBe(false);
727	  });
728	
729	  test('root itself establishes the positioned ancestor the stretched-link overlay resolves against', () => {
730	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({});
731	    expect((style.root as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('relative');
732	  });
733	
734	  /**
735	   * Fix E (full-sweep follow-up audit): price's "hidden by default" half used to be an
736	   * unconditional root-level rule here — this test asserted exactly that shape before the fix.
737	   * Moved inside HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY instead (mirroring notify-me's own Fix C shape), because an
738	   * unconditional hide left Home's price permanently invisible on a touch pointer (confirmed live:
739	   * the Home story showed no price at all at mobile widths) — Mobile has no Hover variant at all
740	   * to ever reveal it. `root[PRICE_KEY]` must now be undefined; the hide lives at
741	   * `hoverBlock[PRICE_KEY]` instead.
742	   */
743	  test('home (hoverRevealsPrice): price has NO unconditional rule (stays visible on touch), hides+reveals only inside HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY, no size-selector rule at all', () => {
744	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({ hoverRevealsPrice: true });
745	    const root = style.root as Record<string, unknown>;
746	    expect(root[PRICE_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
747	    const hoverBlock = root[HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY] as Record<string, unknown>;
748	    // Fix J (SFCC-236): was `display: 'none'`/`'block'` at all three keys below — hidden/revealed
749	    // are now expressed via `position`/`clipPath` (see docblock point 3/6's own Fix J note) so a
750	    // hover-capable pointer that isn't currently hovering/focus-visible still leaves price in the
751	    // DOM/tab order/accessibility tree, just visually clipped.
752	    expect((hoverBlock[PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('absolute');
753	    expect((hoverBlock[PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('inset(50%)');
754	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('static');
755	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('none');
756	    // Fix 2 (Scorer rework round 1): the focus-visible equivalent must reveal identically, so a
757	    // keyboard-only user tabbing through the card sees the same state a mouse-hover would.
758	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('static');
759	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('none');
760	    expect(root[SIZE_CHIPS_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
761	    expect(hoverBlock[HOVER_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
762	    expect(hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
763	  });
764	
765	  test('plp/wishlist (hoverHidesPrice + hoverRevealsSizeSelector): price visible by default, size-selector hidden by default, both swap on hover AND on focus-visible', () => {
766	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({ hoverHidesPrice: true, hoverRevealsSizeSelector: true });
767	    const root = style.root as Record<string, unknown>;
768	    // No unconditional price rule — Content's own natural rendering already shows it by default.
769	    expect(root[PRICE_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
770	    // Fix J (SFCC-236) converted this unconditional (outside HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY) rule from
771	    // `display: 'none'` to `position`/`clipPath`, on the reasoning that it's the paired hidden
772	    // state for the hover/focus-visible reveal below it. Fix K (CodeRabbit finding on PR #85,
773	    // verified correct before fixing) reverted that: unlike price/notify-me's own unconditional
774	    // rules, THIS one is not scoped to "not yet revealed on a pointer type that CAN reveal it" —
775	    // it applies on every pointer type, including touch, which never enters HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY at
776	    // all. Clip-path here left a real, always-tabbable `<button>` (each ZimmSizeChip's own roving
777	    // tabindex) permanently reachable by Tab on a touch device with no way to ever reveal it. Back
778	    // to `display: 'none'` unconditionally; the hover-capable override (asserted just below, on
779	    // `hoverBlock`) is what now carries the Fix J clip-path technique instead.
780	    expect(root[SIZE_CHIPS_KEY]).toEqual({ display: 'none' });
781	    const hoverBlock = root[HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY] as Record<string, unknown>;
782	    // Fix K: the hover-capable override — this pointer type genuinely CAN reveal the content
783	    // below, so it needs the Fix J clip-path technique (stay in the DOM/tab order while not yet
784	    // revealed) instead of the unconditional display:none above.
785	    expect((hoverBlock[SIZE_CHIPS_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).display).toBe('flex');
786	    expect((hoverBlock[SIZE_CHIPS_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('absolute');
787	    expect((hoverBlock[SIZE_CHIPS_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('inset(50%)');
788	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('absolute');
789	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('inset(50%)');
790	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('static');
791	    expect((hoverBlock[HOVER_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('none');
792	    // Fix 2 (Scorer rework round 1): focus-visible must swap identically to hover — a keyboard
793	    // user tabbing into the card (e.g. onto the bag button or a size chip) sees the size-selector
794	    // in place of the price, the same revealed state a mouse-hover produces, not a silently
795	    // unreachable one.
796	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('absolute');
797	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_PRICE_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('inset(50%)');
798	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).position).toBe('static');
799	    expect((hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY] as Record<string, unknown>).clipPath).toBe('none');
800	  });
801	
802	  test('with every hover flag false/absent, no hover-reveal or focus-visible-reveal rule is emitted at all — a touch/no-hover pointer keeps the natural default permanently', () => {
803	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({});
804	    const root = style.root as Record<string, unknown>;
805	    expect(root[PRICE_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
806	    expect(root[SIZE_CHIPS_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
807	    const hoverBlock = (root[HOVER_CAPABLE_QUERY] ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>;
808	    expect(hoverBlock[HOVER_PRICE_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
809	    expect(hoverBlock[HOVER_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
810	    expect(hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_PRICE_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
811	    expect(hoverBlock[FOCUS_VISIBLE_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY]).toBeUndefined();
812	  });
813	
814	  /**
815	   * Fix C (found during the SFCC-236 Step 6 visual audit): confirmed against the real Figma
816	   * Default+Hover Unavailable instances for every variation (desktop and mobile) that an
817	   * out-of-stock item must NOT get the price/size-selector swap, and that the size-chip wrapper
818	   * stays hidden PERMANENTLY (not just "not swapped in on hover") — index.tsx is responsible for
819	   * AND-ing `hoverHidesPrice`/`hoverRevealsSizeSelector` with `!isUnavailable`, and separately
820	   * computing `sizeSelectorUnavailable` to carry that permanent hide, before any of it reaches
821	   * this recipe. This test passes the exact shape a real `variation: 'plp', isUnavailable: true`
822	   * card would produce, alongside `hoverRevealsNotifyMe: true` (what `showNotifyMe` resolves to
823	   * for that same card once `onNotifyMe` is supplied).
824	   *
825	   * Fix F (full-sweep follow-up audit) revises this test's own price expectations: it used to
826	   * assert `root[PRICE_KEY]` was undefined ("price only ever shown via Content's own natural
827	   * rendering, never touched by this recipe at all"). That was true on Desktop but wrong on
828	   * Mobile — Figma's Mobile PLP/Wishlist Unavailable references hide price entirely (swapped for
829	   * notify-me), unlike Desktop's own additive treatment. `sizeSelectorUnavailable` now also
830	   * carries a mobile-hidden/desktop-shown price rule, asserted below.
831	   */
832	  test('unavailable PLP: no desktop price swap, size-chips permanently hidden, price hidden on mobile only, notify-me still hover-gates', () => {
833	    const style = ZimmProductCardRecipe.baseStyle({
834	      hoverHidesPrice: false,
835	      hoverRevealsPrice: false,
836	      hoverRevealsSizeSelector: false,
837	      hoverRevealsNotifyMe: true,
838	      sizeSelectorUnavailable: true,
839	    });
840	    const root = style.root as Record<string, unknown>;
841	    // Both price and size-chips get an unconditional (mobile-first) rule now — a permanent hide
842	    // for size-chips (no reveal anywhere), and a mobile-only hide for price (reveals again at
843	    // DESKTOP_QUERY, asserted further below).

